--!nocheck
-- Prepares ChatGPT's model packs after File > Import 3D, for the Studio command bar.
-- Generated by scripts/generate-prepare.py from the packs' model_manifest.json files: edit
-- scripts/PrepareChatGPTModels.template.luau and run that, not the generated file.
--
-- 1. File > Import 3D, every pack's combined .gltf at once (Creator: Big Dink Studios, Scale Unit:
--    Meter, World Forward: Back, since the packs face -Z). For the high-poly pass they're in
--    ~/Desktop/LawnModelsImport/HighPoly/ALL, with their textures beside it in ../Textures.
-- 2. Paste this into the command bar. It finds every imported model, works out from each pack's
--    grid layout whether Studio turned it around, puts each model's origin at the world origin in
--    the manifest's frame, and adds:
--      * the Handle (tools) or Root part
--      * the BedArea and BaySpot parts, and the manifests' marker Attachments (Mount, FloorSpot,
--        Desk, DeliverySpot, TruckParking, DriverSeat, UseSpot, ScreenView, Contents, SnapL...)
--        with their attributes
--      * each part's collision from the manifest, and a pivot on the hinge for the parts that
--        swing or spin (doors, tailgates, ramps, flaps), since the importer centres every pivot
--    then stages them in ServerStorage.ModelImport.<Folder>.
-- 3. Right-click ServerStorage.ModelImport > Save / Export > Save to File, and run
--    `lune run scripts/export-models <file> --overwrite` to write assets/<Folder>/*.rbxm.
-- 4. Delete ServerStorage.ModelImport.

